'''Morseerians''' were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] native to the [[planet]] [[Merj]].

==Biology and appearance==
Morseerians<ref name="Complete Locations">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] native to the [[planet]] [[Merj]],<ref name="Catalyst" /> that had elongated, conical heads, four [[Limb|arms]],<ref name="ANH" /> and a [[methane]]-based [[Methane breather|respiration]]. Morseerians were unable to distinguish [[human]] faces.<ref name="Catalyst" /> Morseerians had to wear special suits and [[Breath mask|gas masks]] when traveling to [[oxygen]]-based planets.<ref name="Alien Archive">''[[Star Wars: Alien Archive]]''</ref> Morseerians had [[Color|green]]<ref name="ANH" /> or blue skin,<ref name="The Missing Agent" /> though the skin underneath their suits was translucent.<ref name="Catalyst" />

==History==
Morseerians were a secretive species and as such not much was known about the history, or culture of the species<ref name="Alien Archive" /> It was known however that they hailed from the planet [[Merj]].<ref name="Catalyst" /> Some Morseerians have gained fame in the wider galaxy, including Nabrun Leids.<ref name="Alien Archive" />

==Morseerians in the Galaxy==

===High republic era===
The Morseerian [[Gluth Andoi]] was a [[Jedi Master]] of the [[Jedi Order]] during the [[High Republic Era]]. He also served on the [[Jedi High Council|High Jedi Council]]. He would go on to perish on [[Dalna]] in the [[Night of Sorrow|Battle of Dalna]] against the [[Path of the Open Hand]]. Andoi was struck by [[blaster]] [[Laser|fire]] and subsequently turned to stone by the [[Great Leveler|Leveler]]<ref name="Path of Vengeance">''[[The High Republic: Path of Vengeance]]''</ref> in 382 BBY.<ref name="AndoiDate">''[[The High Republic: Path of Vengeance]]'' establishes that Gluth Andoi [[Death|died]] on [[Dalna]] during the [[Night of Sorrow]], which ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates to [[382 BBY]].</ref>

[[File:MorseerianPirateYJA.png|thumb|left|150px|A Morseerian pirate who served under Sellac Orryak.]]
In 232 BBY<ref name="211ADate">{{YJADate|211A}}</ref> at least one Morseerian pirate served under [[Sellaccc Orryak]] with the [[Ganguls]] and was present for the [[Takeover of Yarrum Tower]].<ref name="Tower Run">{{YJA|Tower Run}}</ref>Another was present in [[Yarrum Tower]] at the time of the [[Raid on Vuundalla]].<ref name="Unmasked">{{YJA|Unmasked}}</ref> Later in Yarrum Tower a Morseerian was present with an aggravated [[Dwuni]].<ref name="Spaceport Setback">{{YJA|The Spaceport Setback}}</ref> A Morseerian [[pirate]] was also present during the attempted takeover of the [[Tenoo Jedi Temple]] during the [[Battle of Tenoo]]<ref name="BOT">{{YJA|The Battle of Tenoo}}</ref>

According to a [[Joria Skarl's holocron|Holocron]] recorded by the Jedi explorer [[Joria Skarl]] and stored in the [[Jedi Archives]], she visited a [[Phoolian Monks monastery|monastery]] of the [[Phoolian Monks]] order on the [[planet]] [[Bartool]] during which she learned of the story of [[Darth Ravi]] the Bold. In the story two Morseerian followers of Darth Ravi were searching for the [[Echo Stone]], an artefact that had been sealed inside a complex puzzle created by the [[Ancients (Echo Stone)|Ancients]] on the [[Dead Moon of Gothol]]. One of the Morseerians would fall victim to a trap laid by the Ancients in which he fell into a hole. The other Morseerian died on that moon as well.<ref name="Echoes of Fear 1">[[The High Republic Adventures – Echoes of Fear 1|''The High Republic Adventures – Echoes of Fear'' 1]]</ref> [[Chell Trambin]] was a Morseerian [[Nihil]] who lived during the [[High Republic Era]]. He would later [[Death|perish]] during the [[Second Battle of Cyclor]].<ref name="Rising Storm">''[[The High Republic: The Rising Storm]]''</ref> Another Morseerian was present in the [[Steebark District]] eating at [[Groneman's|Groneman's diner]] when [[Sian Holt]] was tracking [[Urk Panga]].<ref name="TOS 1">[[The High Republic: Trail of Shadows 1|''The High Republic: Trail of Shadows'' 1]]</ref>

Multiple Morseerian [[scientist]]s worked for the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] during the [[Clone Wars]], including [[Nan Pakota]] and [[Urshe Torr]]. They were tasked with overseeing the creation of a [[biological warfare]] agent that would affect the [[clone trooper]]s in the [[Grand Army of the Republic]]. [[Galactic Republic]] [[Lieutenant Commander]] [[Orson Callan Krennic|Orson Krennic]] undertook a [[Mission to Merj|mission]] to Merj to capture the scientists and then use them in a [[prisoner]] [[Vallt Rescue Operation|exchange]] on [[Vallt]].<ref name="Catalyst" /> Sometime Between [[24 BBY]] and [[22 BBY]],<ref name="HyperspaceStories6Date">{{HyperspaceStories6Date}}</ref> a Morseerian was present at [[Boba Fett's Palace|Jabba's Palace]] during a circus performance during which [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure|Jabba]] showcased the [[Sunburst Gem]].<ref name="Hyperspace Stories 6">[[Hyperspace Stories 6|''Hyperspace Stories'' 6]]</ref>

===Imperial era===
During the reign of the Empire, A group of Morseerian pirates operated a ship that employed the [[WDD adminmech droid|WDD adminmech]] droid [[DD-BD]] prior to the droid’s sale into [[slavery]]. The Morseerian pirate ship was impounded by the [[Galactic Empire]], after which the droid was auctioned to the [[Pyke Syndicate]].<ref name="DD databank">{{Databank|dd-bd|DD-BD}}</ref> Between [[19 BBY]] and [[9 BBY]]<ref name="Star Wars (2015) 28 Obi-Wan flashback">The secondary flashback in this issue depicts [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] during his exile on [[Tatooine]], which began in [[19 BBY]], seen in {{Film|III}} which is dated by ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''. Obi-Wan Kenobi is also visibly younger than his appearance in the opening flashback in [[Star Wars (2015) 27]], which occurs during [[8 BBY]] and [[1 BBY]]. Therefore, the flashback must occur between ''Star Wars'': Episode III ''Revenge of the Sith'' and the opening flashback in [[Star Wars (2015)]] 27, which correlates to between 19 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|BBY]] and 9 BBY.</ref> a A Morseerian was present within the streets of Mos Eisley when [[Obi-Wan Kenobi|Ben Kenobi]] noticed a man with a spiral on his forehead.<ref name="Star Wars 28">[[Star Wars (2015) 28|''Star Wars'' (2015) 28]]</ref> In [[2 BBY]]<ref name="FRDate">"Final Round" features the ''[[Phantom II]]'', which first appeared in "[[The Last Battle]]," and it also mentions [[Jun Sato]], who died in "[[Zero Hour]]." ''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]'' places "The Last Battle" seventeen [[Standard year|years]] after the end of the [[Clone Wars]], which ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates to [[19 BBY]], meaning that "The Last Battle" takes place in [[2 BBY]]. ''[[Star Wars: Battles that Changed the Galaxy]]'' places the events of "Zero Hour" 17 [[Standard year|years]] after the [[Proclamation of the New Order|formation]] of the [[Galactic Empire]], which occurred in [[19 BBY]] according to ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'', meaning that "Zero Hour" takes place in 2 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|BBY]], and "Final Round" takes place in the same year.</ref> a Morseerian was kept [[prisoner]] on [[Starlag XIX]]. The Morseerian and other prisoners trampled guards when an explosion caused by [[Tonk]] caused all of their collars to disengage.<ref name="Final Round">{{RebelsMagCite|34|Final Round}}</ref>

[[File:MorseerianOrphanGOTW.png|thumb|right|200px|A juvenile Morseerian orphan in class.]]
Morseerians were among the species of orphans sheltered in the improvised orphanage run by [[Killi Gimm]] and [[Kaya Gimm]]. Kaya's former droid-repair home was turned into an [[Gimm sisters' orphanage|orphanage]] near the Midwalls of [[Jedha City]] following the Imperial occupation. The caregivers had to learn and accommodate the specific atmospheric requirements of Morseerian children.<ref name="GotW">[[Guardians of the Whills (novel)|''Guardians of the Whills'']]</ref> A Juvenile Morseerian was instructed within a class taught by Kaya.<ref name="Manga">''[[Guardians of the Whills: The Manga]]''</ref>

Between [[2 BBY]] and [[1 BBY]]<ref name="TSWPDate">"The Sand Will Provide" takes place after the formation of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]], but prior to [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]]'s [[death]], which ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas: Updated Edition]]'' dates to [[1 BBY]]. ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the formation of the Rebel Alliance to [[2 BBY]]. Therefore, "The Sand Will Provide" takes place in between 2 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|BBY]] and 1 BBY.</ref> a Morseerian was present within Chalmun's Spaceport Cantina when a young [[Tusken Raider]] attempted entry.<ref name="The Sand Will Provide">{{StoryCite|story=The Sand Will Provide|book=Star Wars (2015) 37}}</ref> A Morseerian was Present within Chalmun's Spaceport Cantina playing [[Sabacc]] with a [[Devaronian]] and a [[Talz]] during a bounty hunting trip [[Bossk'wassak'Cradossk|Bossk]] took on [[Tatooine]].<ref name="Bounty Hunt">''[[Bounty Hunt]]''</ref>

Shortly before the [[Battle of Yavin]], a [[Gender|male]] Morseerian named [[Nabrun Leids]], attended [[Chalmun's Spaceport Cantina|the cantina]] of [[Mos Eisley]] the [[Standard day|day]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and [[Luke Skywalker]] met [[Han Solo]] and [[Chewbacca]].<ref name="EYNTK" /> Leids was also present within the cantina when [[Boba Fett]] questioned patrons about [[Luke Skywalker]] shortly after he blew up the [[Death Star]].<ref name="Star Wars 5">[[Star Wars (2015) 5|''Star Wars'' (2015) 5]]</ref> Many years later, Leids was present on [[Oba Diah]], where he told [[Karr Nuq Sin]] about Skywalker and Kenobi's appearance at the cantina, though Leids did not remember what planet it had occurred on.<ref name="FC">''[[Force Collector]]''</ref>

A Morseerian was among those in a [[Unidentified bar (Nar Shaddaa)|bar]] on [[Nar Shaddaa]] who attempted to beat up [[Luke Skywalker]] but was frightened back when Luke ignited out his [[Lightsaber]].<ref name="Star Wars 8">[[Star Wars (2015) 8|''Star Wars'' (2015) 8]]</ref> Shortly before a [[Skirmish on Hubin]] a Morseerian was present within a cantina on [[Hubin]] during a shootout between Han Solo and a Hubin native.<ref name="Star Wars 59">[[Star Wars (2015) 59|''Star Wars'' (2015) 59]]</ref> Later a Morseerian was present within a bar on [[Carajam]] after shortly after the [[Showdown on Carajam]].<ref name="Age of Rebellion">[[Age of Rebellion - Boba Fett 1|''Age of Rebellion - Boba Fett'' 1]]</ref>

===New republic era===

A Morseerian served as a crew member aboard the [[Buried Treasure]] and shared a bunk with [[Yrica Quell]] in alternating shifts. The Morseerian occupied the bunk when Quell was on duty as an [[Intelligence analyst]].<ref name="Alphabet">[[Alphabet Squadron (novel)|''Alphabet Squadron'']]</ref> 

[[File:MorseerianSusVarkana.png|thumb|left|250px|A Morseerian on Varkana notices Kazuda Xiono.]]
[[Lourgh T'oknell]] was a Morseerian pilot who served in the [[New Republic]]’s [[Alphabet Squadron]] and later in [[Flare Squadron]] under [[Wyl Lark]]’s command. He was killed in action when his fighter was lost during a failed attempt to prevent a group of [[TIE/ln space superiority starfighter|TIE fighters]] from jumping to [[lightspeed]]. Prior to his death, T'oknell had been scheduled to meet with Wyl Lark and had been working with him to retrofit a bunk bed to accommodate his six limbs aboard the [[Deliverance]]. The [[Lourgh T'oknell's brother|brother]] of Lourgh served as a communications officer aboard a New Republic vessel and wore a respirator mask. He granted Wyl Lark unauthorized access to a comm room, explaining that who his brother was and that Wyl had been kind to him. While nervously adjusting his respirator mask, the Morseerian asked “Is that all?” after Wyl finished recording a message, then agreed without hesitation to Wyl’s request to forward any incoming signal from Yrica Quell and [[Kairos]] to [[Chass na Chadic]] and [[Nath Tensent]].<ref name="Victory's Price">''[[Victory's Price: An Alphabet Squadron Novel]]''</ref>

In [[34 ABY]]<ref name="34 ABY">{{ResistanceDate|2|12}}</ref> Several Morseerians were present on [[Varkana]] during the [[Rescue of Norath Kev]]. One of the Morseerians looked at [[Kazuda Xiono]], [[CB-23]] and [[Jarek Yeager]] when they walked down a street in search of [[Norath Kev]].<ref name="The Missing Agent" />

==Behind the scenes==
Morseerians first appeared in the [[1977]] film [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']], the first installment of the ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[original trilogy]].<ref name="A New Hope">{{Film|IV}}</ref> 

[[File:PossibleSenatorsHostageChisisArt.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Concept art for a Morseerian senator, here misspelled as Moressian.]]
The head of the [[Rodian]] originally fit the head of a four-armed creature named the "Plutonian." This creature was later known as a Morseerian.<ref name="Much to learn">{{SW|url=news/much-to-learn-you-still-have-9-things-you-might-not-know-about-rodians|text=Much to Learn You Still Have: 9 Things You Might Not Know About Rodians}}</ref> The Morseerian first appeared as a cantina alien in [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']]. During the film's production, Leids' species was listed as "Plutonian" by [[John Mollo]].<ref name="Art Of Star Wars">''[[The Art of Star Wars Episode IV: A New Hope]]''</ref> According to [[Tom Spina]], in the film, Leids was portrayed by an actress named [[Diana Sadley Way]], who was also listed in Mollo's notes.<ref name="Tom Spina Leids E-Mail">{{EmailCite|email=File:DianSadleyWayPProof.png|creator=Tom Spina|date=2021-06-12}}</ref><ref name="Art Of Star Wars" /> At one point Morseerians were considered for the role of a senator in [[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]] episode [[Hostage Crisis]]. [[Russell G. Chong]] created concept art for a Morseerian senator.{{WebCite|url=https://www.artrgcportfolio.com/starwarstheclonewars|text=Star Wars The Clone Wars Lucasfilm Animation Ltd.|author=Russel Chong|archivedate=20251203011921}}

